027-520D-497F-9052-63EC199F5E63\" target=\"new\">Historical Public Debt Database<\/a>","title":"Historical Public Debt Database","intro4":"Send us your comments about <div><u><a href=\"mailto:datamapper@imf.org\">DataMapper Tool<\/a><\/u><\/div> <br>\r\n\r\nSend us your comments about <div><a href=\"mailto:DataMapper@imf.org\"><u>DataMapper Tool<\/u><\/a><\/div>","projectionyear":"2015","caption3":"Methodology","indicatorx":"DEBT1","maxyear":"2015","version":"IMF 2017","indicatory":"DEBT1","maparea":"FAD_WORLD","intro1":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/pubs\/cat\/longres.cfm?sk=24332.0 \" target=\"new\">IMF Working Paper - A Historical Public Debt Database<\/a>","hierarchies":{"indicators":{"1":{"label":"Historical Public Debt Database","indicators":["DEBT1"]}},"groups":{"1":"FAD_WORLD","2":"FAD_G20Adv","3":"FAD_G20Emg","4":"FAD_LIC"}},"numcountries":235,"geoitems":["ABW",null,"AFG","AGO","AIA","ALB","ARE","ARG","ARM","ASM","ATG","AUS","AUT","AZE","BDI","BEL","BEN","BFA","BGD","BGR","BHR","BHS","BIH","BLR","BLZ","BMU","BOL","BRA","BRB","BRN","BTN","BWA","CAF","CAN","CHE","CHI","CHL","CHN","CIV","CMR","COD","COG","COK","COL","COM","CPV","CRI","CUB","CUW","CYM","CYP","CZE","DEU","DJI","DMA","DNK","DOM","DZA","ECU","EGY","ERI","ESH","ESP","EST","ETH","FIN","FJI","FLK","FRA","FRO","FSM","GAB","GBR","GEO","GHA","GIB","GIN","GLP","GMB","GNB","GNQ","GRC","GRD","GRL","GTM","GUF","GUM","GUY","HKG","HND","HRV","HTI","HUN","IDN","IMY","IND","IRL","IRN","IRQ","ISL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JOR","JPN","KAZ","KEN","KGZ","KHM","KIR","KNA","KOR","KWT","LAO","LBN","LBR","LBY","LCA","LIE","LKA","LSO","LTU","LUX","LVA","MAC","MAR","MCO","MDA","MDG","MDV","MEX","MHL","MKD","MLI","MLT","MMR","MNE","MNG","MNP","MOZ","MRT","MSR","MTQ","MUS","MWI","MYS","MYT","NAM","NCL","NER","NGA","NIC","NIU","NLD","NOR","NPL","NRU","NZL","OMN","PAK","PAN","PCN","PER","PHL","PLW","PNG","POL","PRI","PRK","PRT","PRY","PYF","QAT","REU","ROU","RUS","RWA","SAU","SDN","SEN","SGP","SHN","SJM","SLB","SLE","SLV","SMR","SOM","SPM","SRB","SSD","STP","SUR","SVK","SVN","SWE","SWZ","SXM","SYC","SYR","TCA","TCD","TGO","THA","TJK","TKL","TKM","TLS","TON","TTO","TUN","TUR","TUV","TWN","TZA","UGA","UKR","URY","USA",null,"UZB","VAT","VCT","VEN","VGB","VIR","VNM","VUT","WBG","WLF","WSM","YEM","ZAF","ZMB","ZWE"],"regions":{"FAD_WORLD":["ABW","ADO","AFG","AGO","AIA","ALB","ARE","ARG","ARM","ASM","ATG","AUS","AUT","AZE","BDI","BEL","BEN","BFA","BGD","BGR","BHR","BHS","BIH","BLR","BLZ","BMU","BOL","BRA","BRB","BRN","BTN","BWA","CAF","CAN","CHE","CHI","CHL","CHN","CIV","CMR","COD","COG","COK","COL","COM","CPV","CRI","CUB","CUW","CYM","CYP","CZE","DEU","DJI","DMA","DNK","DOM","DZA","ECU","EGY","ERI","ESH","ESP","EST","ETH","FIN","FJI","FLK","FRA","FRO","FSM","GAB","GBR","GEO","GHA","GIB","GIN","GLP","GMB","GNB","GNQ","GRC","GRD","GRL","GTM","GUF","GUM","GUY","HKG","HND","HRV","HTI","HUN","IDN","IMY","IND","IRL","IRN","IRQ","ISL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JOR","JPN","KAZ","KEN","KGZ","KHM","KIR","KNA","KOR","KWT","LAO","LBN","LBR","LBY","LCA","LIE","LKA","LSO","LTU","LUX","LVA","MAC","MAR","MCO","MDA","MDG","MDV","MEX","MHL","MKD","MLI","MLT","MMR","MNE","MNG","MNP","MOZ","MRT","MSR","MTQ","MUS","MWI","MYS","MYT","NAM","NCL","NER","NGA","NIC","NIU","NLD","NOR","NPL","NRU","NZL","OMN","PAK","PAN","PCN","PER","PHL","PLW","PNG","POL","PRI","PRK","PRT","PRY","PYF","QAT","REU","ROU","RUS","RWA","SAU","SDN","SEN","SGP","SHN","SJM","SLB","SLE","SLV","SMR","SOM","SPM","SRB","SSD","STP","SUR","SVK","SVN","SWE","SWZ","SXM","SYC","SYR","TCA","TCD","TGO","THA","TJK","TKL","TKM","TLS","TON","TTO","TUN","TUR","TUV","TWN","TZA","UGA","UKR","URY","USA","UVK","UZB","VAT","VCT","VEN","VGB","VIR","VNM","VUT","WBG","WLF","WSM","YEM","ZAF","ZMB","ZWE"],"FAD_G20Emg":["ARG","BRA","CHN","IDN","IND","MEX","RUS","SAU","TUR","ZAF"],"FAD_G20Adv":["AUS","CAN","DEU","FRA","GBR","ITA","JPN","KOR","USA"],"FAD_LIC":["BDI","BEN","BFA","BGD","BOL","BTN","CAF","CIV","CMR","COD","COG","COM","CPV","DJI","DMA","ERI","ETH","GHA","GIN","GMB","GNB","GRD","GUY","HND","HTI","KGZ","KHM","LAO","LBR","LCA","LSO","MDA","MDG","MDV","MLI","MMR","MNG","MOZ","MRT","MWI","NER","NIC","NPL","PNG","RWA","SDN","SEN","SLB","SLE","STP","TCD","TGO","TJK","TON","TZA","UGA","UZB","VCT","VUT","WSM","YEM","ZMB","ZWE"]}},"CF":{"order":"11","code":"CF","description":"Low-income countries (LICs) are typically characterized by intermittent and very modest access to private external funding sources. Motivated by recent developments in private flows to LICs the following dataset on gross private capital flows was constructed with special focus on non-FDI flows in LICs. Concentrating on LICs and more specifically on gross non-FDI private flows is intentionally aimed at closing a gap in existing datasets where country coverage of developing economies is limited mainly to emerging markets (EMs). The newly constructed dataset covers 58 LICs and 92 EMs for the period of 1990 to 2012. The primary data source used to build the dataset is the Balance of Payments Statistics (BOPS) dataset, following the compilation methodology described in the IMF\u2019s Balance of Payments Manual version 6 (BPM6).\r\n+B4Non-FDI Capital Inflows in Low-Income Developing Countries: Catching the Wave?  https:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/pubs\/ft\/wp\/2015\/wp1586.pdf\r\nAuthor\/Editor:  Juliana Dutra Araujo ; Antonio David ; Carlos van Hombeeck ; Chris Papageorgiou  \r\nPublication Date:  April 29, 2015  \r\n                        \r\n","caption2":"Dataset","caption3":"Methodology","intro4":"Send comments and questions to the <div><a href=\"mailto:CF_in_LICs@imf.org\"><u>Capital Flows Data<\/u><\/a><\/div> <br>\r\n\r\nSend us your comments about <div>\r\n<a href=\"mailto:DataMapper@imf.org\"><u>DataMapper Tool<\/u><\/a><\/div> \r\n","indicator":"DirectAbroad","intro3":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/datamapper\/CF_meta.xlsx\" target=\"new\">LIC Country Level Notes<\/a>\r\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/pp\/eng\/2014\/060314.pdf\" target=\"new\">LIC Country Group Classifications<\/a>","bubbleresize_ind":"LP,NGDPD","caption1":"Relevant paper","intro1":"<a href=\"https:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/pubs\/ft\/wp\/2015\/wp1586.pdf\" target=\"new\">Catching the Wave: Non FDI Capital Inflows<\/a>\r\n<a href=\"http:\/\/itunes.apple.com\/us\/app\/imf-news-and-data-for-the-ipad\/id414587764?mt=8\" target=\"new\">Also available on iPad<\/a>","projectionyear":"2020","caption4":"Feedback","maxyear":"2014","indicatorx":"NGDPD","sdmx_geoitem ":"REF_AREA","initchart":"SPR_LIDC","indicatory":"LP","intro2":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/datamapper\/CF_data.xlsx\" target=\"new\">Full Data<\/a>","title":"Capital Flows in Developing Economies (April 2016)","maparea":"CFWORLD","minyear":"1995","sdmx_freq ":"FREQ","version":"Capital Flows in Developing Economies (April 2016)","hierarchies":{"indicators":{"1":{"label":"Direct Investment","indicators":["DirectAbroad","DirectIn"]},"2":{"indicators":["PrivInexDI","PrivInexDIGDP","PrivOutexDI","PrivOutexDIGDP"],"label":"Private Flows excluding Direct Investment "},"3":{"indicators":["Portfa","Portfl","EquityA","EquityL","DebtA","DebtL"],"label":"By Type of Private Flow - Portfolio"},"4":{"indicators":["OtherGov","OtherA","OtherL"],"label":"By Type of Private Flow - Other Investment"},"5":{"indicators":["Deriv","DebtForg","GDP"],"label":"Other"}},"groups":{"1":{"code":"CFWORLD","groups":{"1":"SPR_HIC","2":"SPR_LIDC"}}}},"numcountries":174,"geoitems":["AFG","ALB","DZA","AGO","ATG","ARG","ARM","AUS","AUT","AZE","BHS","BHR","BGD","BRB","BLR","BEL","BLZ","BEN","BTN","BOL","BWA","BRA","BGR","BFA","BDI","KHM","CAN","CAF","TCD","CHL","CHN","COL","COM","COD","COG","CRI","CIV","HRV","CYP","CZE","DNK","DJI","DMA","DOM","ECU","EGY","SLV","GNQ","EST","ETH","FJI","FIN","FRA","GAB","GMB","GEO","DEU","GHA","GRC","GRD","GTM","GIN","GNB","GUY","HTI","HND","HKG","HUN","ISL","IND","IDN","IRN","IRQ","IRL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JPN","JOR","KAZ","KEN","KOR","KWT","KGZ","LAO","LVA","LBN","LBR","LTU","LUX","MKD","MDG","MWI","MYS","MDV","MLI","MLT","MRT","MUS","MEX","MDA","MNG","MAR","MOZ","MMR","NAM","NPL","NLD","NZL","NIC","NER","NGA","NOR","OMN","PAK","PAN","PNG","PRY","PER","PHL","POL","PRT","QAT","ROU","RUS","RWA","WSM","SAU","SEN","SRB","SYC","SLE","SGP","SVK","SVN","SLB","ZAF","ESP","LKA","KNA","VCT","SDN","SUR","SWZ","SWE","CHE","SYR","TJK","TZA","THA","TGO","TON","TTO","TUN","TUR","UGA","UKR","ARE","GBR","USA","URY","UZB","VUT","VEN","VNM","YEM","ZMB","ZWE","ERI","KIR","LSO","STP","SOM","SSD"],"regions":{"CFWORLD":["AFG","ALB","DZA","AGO","ATG","ARG","ARM","AUS","AUT","AZE","BHS","BHR","BGD","BRB","BLR","BEL","BLZ","BEN","BTN","BOL","BWA","BRA","BGR","BFA","BDI","KHM","CAN","CAF","TCD","CHL","CHN","COL","COM","COD","COG","CRI","CIV","HRV","CYP","CZE","DNK","DJI","DMA","DOM","ECU","EGY","SLV","GNQ","EST","ETH","FJI","FIN","FRA","GAB","GMB","GEO","DEU","GHA","GRC","GRD","GTM","GIN","GNB","GUY","HTI","HND","HKG","HUN","ISL","IND","IDN","IRN","IRQ","IRL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JPN","JOR","KAZ","KEN","KOR","KWT","KGZ","LAO","LVA","LBN","LBR","LTU","LUX","MKD","MDG","MWI","MYS","MDV","MLI","MLT","MRT","MUS","MEX","MDA","MNG","MAR","MOZ","MMR","NAM","NPL","NLD","NZL","NIC","NER","NGA","NOR","OMN","PAK","PAN","PNG","PRY","PER","PHL","POL","PRT","QAT","ROU","RUS","RWA","WSM","SAU","SEN","SRB","SYC","SLE","SGP","SVK","SVN","SLB","ZAF","ESP","LKA","KNA","VCT","SDN","SUR","SWZ","SWE","CHE","SYR","TJK","TZA","THA","TGO","TON","TTO","TUN","TUR","UGA","UKR","ARE","GBR","USA","URY","UZB","VUT","VEN","VNM","YEM","ZMB","ZWE","ERI","KIR","LSO","STP","SOM","SSD"],"SPR_LIDC":["AFG","BGD","BEN","BTN","BOL","BFA","BDI","KHM","CAF","TCD","COM","COD","COG","CIV","DJI","ETH","GMB","GHA","GIN","GNB","HTI","HND","KEN","KGZ","LAO","LBR","MDG","MWI","MLI","MRT","MDA","MNG","MOZ","MMR","NPL","NIC","NER","NGA","PNG","RWA","SEN","SLE","SLB","SDN","TJK","TZA","TGO","UGA","UZB","VNM","YEM","ZMB","ZWE","ERI","KIR","LSO","STP","SOM","SSD"],"SPR_HIC":["AUS","AUT","BEL","CAN","CYP","CZE","DNK","EST","FIN","FRA","DEU","GRC","HKG","ISL","IRL","ISR","ITA","JPN","KOR","LVA","LUX","MLT","NLD","NZL","NOR","PRT","SGP","SVK","SVN","ESP","SWE","CHE","GBR","USA"]}},"SPRLU":{"code":"SPRLU","order":"12","intro4":"Send us your comments about <div><a href=\"mailto:DataMapper@imf.org\"><u>DataMapper Tool<\/u><\/a><\/div> <br>","indicatory":"intensive","caption1":"Export Diversification Papers","indicator":"total_theil","caption2":"IMF-DFID Collaboration","maparea":"WEOWORLD","title":"Export Diversification and Quality (July 2017)","caption4":"Feedback","description":"Covering 198 countries including most low-income countries, the toolkit provides indicators on export product diversification and export product quality from 1962-2014. The measures in this toolkit are calculated based on an updated version of the UN\u2013NBER dataset, which harmonizes COMTRADE bilateral trade flow data at the 4-digit SITC (Rev. 1) level. The UN\u2013NBER dataset combines importer- and exporter-reported data to maximize comprehensiveness while ensuring internal consistency, using the methodology of Asmundson (forthcoming). The export diversification and quality database was developed by IMF staff under a research collaboration between the IMF and the former UK Department for International Development (DFID), which merged with the Foreign & Commonwealth Office (FCO) on September 2, 2020 to become the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO). The team\u2019s working, published, and IMF Board papers on diversification can be found on the project website: <u><a href=\"https:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/res\/dfidimf\/\" target=\"new\">https:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/res\/dfidimf\/<\/a><\/u>.\nThe toolkit includes indices of diversification across export products which can be found under the heading \u201cExport Diversification.\u201d We have three main indicators. The Theil Index provides an overall measure of export diversification. In addition, we have decomposed the overall export diversification index into extensive and intensive margins of diversification. The Extensive Margin reflects the concentration in the number of products by country, while the Intensive Margin component looks at the concentration in the export volumes across active products. Higher values for the all three indices indicate lower diversification.\nThe toolkit also contains export quality measures across different aggregation levels of export products, and these can be found under the \u201cQuality Index\u201d heading. The Export Quality Index measures the overall quality level of each country. The other quality indices measure the sectoral quality levels for each country. For example, \u201cFood and Animals\u201d provides a measure of quality for the food and animals sector. The baseline methodology (see Henn et al. (2013)) estimates quality based on unit values and is a modified version of Hallak (2006). To enable cross-product comparisons, all quality estimates are normalized to their 90th percentile in the relevant product-year combination. The resulting quality values typically range between 0 and 1.2. Higher values for the quality indices indicate higher quality levels. Please see the detailed data description under the Methodology section on the Data Mapper webpage.\nThe data in this toolkit are provided \u201cas is\u201d and \u201cas available,\u201d and every effort is made to ensure, but not guarantee, their timeliness, accuracy, and availability. \nMore granular data from this database are available at the IMF Data website: \n<u><a href=\"https:\/\/data.imf.org\/?sk=A093DF7D-E0B8-4913-80E0-A07CF90B44DB\" target=\"new\">https:\/\/data.imf.org\/?sk=A093DF7D-E0B8-4913-80E0-A07CF90B44DB<\/a><\/u>.","minyear":"1962","caption3":"Methodology","indicatorx":"extensive","maxyear":"2014","version":"July 2017","initchart":"OEMDC,ADVEC,WEOWORLD","intro2":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/res\/dfidimf\/index.htm\" target=\"new\">Macro Research for Development<\/a>\n<a href=\"https:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/res\/dfidimf\/topic4.htm\" target=\"new\">Promoting Structural Change and Institutional Development<\/a>","projectionyear":"2014","intro3":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/pubs\/ft\/weo\/2014\/01\/weodata\/groups.htm\" target=\"new\">Analytical Groups<\/a>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/datamapper\/region.htm\" target=\"new\">Regional Groups<\/a>","intro1":"<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/pp\/eng\/2014\/030514.pdf\" target=\"new\">IMF Policy Paper<\/a>\n<a href=\"http:\/\/www.imf.org\/external\/np\/pp\/eng\/2014\/030514a.pdf\" target=\"new\">Background Notes<\/a>","numcountries":237,"geoitems":["ABW",null,"AFG","AGO","AIA","ALB","ARE","ARG","ARM","ASM","ATG","AUS","AUT","AZE","BDI","BEL","BEN","BFA","BGD","BGR","BHR","BHS","BIH","BLR","BLZ","BMU","BOL","BRA","BRB","BRN","BTN","BWA","CAF","CAN","CHE","CHI","CHL","CHN","CIV","CMR","COD","COG","COK","COL","COM","CPV","CRI","CUB","CUW","CYM","CYP","CZE","DEU","DJI","DMA","DNK","DOM","DZA","ECU","EGY","ERI","ESH","ESP","EST","ETH","FIN","FJI","FLK","FRA","FRO","FSM","GAB","GBR","GEO","GHA","GIB","GIN","GLP","GMB","GNB","GNQ","GRC","GRD","GRL","GTM","GUF","GUM","GUY","HKG","HND","HRV","HTI","HUN","IDN","IMY","IND","IRL","IRN","IRQ","ISL","ISR","ITA","JAM","JOR","JPN","KAZ","KEN","KGZ","KHM","KIR","KNA","KOR","KWT","LAO","LBN","LBR","LBY","LCA","LIE","LKA","LSO","LTU","LUX","LVA","MAC","MAR","MCO","MDA","MDG","MDV","MEX","MHL","MKD","MLI","MLT","MMR","MNE","MNG","MNP","MOZ","MRT","MSR","MTQ","MUS","MWI","MYS","MYT","NAM","NCL","NER","NGA","NIC","NIU","NLD","NOR","NPL","NRU","NZL","OMN","PAK","PAN","PCN","PER","PHL","PLW","PNG","POL","PRI","PRK","PRT","PRY","PYF","QAT","REU","ROU","RUS","RWA","SAU","SDN","SEN","SGP","SHN","SJM","SLB","SLE","SLV","SMR","SOM","SPM","SRB","SSD","STP","SUR","SVK","SVN","SWE","SWZ","SXM","SYC","SYR","TCA","TCD","TGO","THA","TJK","TKL","TKM","TLS","TON","TTO","TUN","TUR","TUV","TWN","TZA"